WEBVTT

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:03.180
Oh, no!

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.520
Let go! Let go!

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:12.190
Keep your hands off those kids!

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.660
Layra!

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.910
Layra!

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.530
D-Wheels.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.850
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.470
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:28.890
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:31.080
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:09.140
Even in Hell, Cards Determine Your Fate

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:11.920
Let me go! Who do you think I am?

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.110
Shut up! Get in already!

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.980
Damn it! I'm telling my daddy about—

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:24.680
Damn...

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:26.590
You two, get in there, too.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:32.330
W-Wait!

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:35.160
Layra... Where's Layra?

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:35.980
Damn you...

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:38.090
Layra! Where are you, Layra?

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:39.440
Pipe down already!

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:41.770
Crow!

00:02:41.770 --> 00:02:43.510
Stop! Don't get any closer!

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:45.520
Hey, guys!

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.980
Don't worry... Make sure you get enough to eat!

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:50.780
Crow! Crow!

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:52.360
Damn it!

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:53.840
Give Crow back!

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.250
Crow!

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.960
Hey, you can hear me, right?

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:00.660
Stop the car! Please!

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:01.990
Calm down, Yuya.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:04.840
But Layra... I have to find Layra!

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:06.740
No need to worry about Layra.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:12.970
It was Tsukikage. In the chaos, I saw him take Layra.

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:15.210
What? Tsukikage took him?

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:19.780
Tsukikage... So he...

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:23.550
Is he another of your friends from another dimension?

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:28.040
Yeah, he was probably looking for us...

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.200
for Layra, on Reiji Akaba's orders.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:33.760
Then, that means he's safe?

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:36.730
That's one bit of good news. It's not all bad.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:40.560
Yes, it is! This is a clear case of mistaken identity!

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.670
I'm telling my daddy, and I'll have you all fired!

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:45.770
Are you listening to me, you jerks?!

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:47.370
You, calm down.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:51.580
Sorry, Shinji. Because you came to let us know...

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:56.860
Well, the one silver lining is that 
the children weren't taken.

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:58.400
Those kids...

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:01.290
I hope they don't resort to stealing food again.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.900
I'm sure our friends on the outside 
will look after them.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:04.860
Yeah.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:08.830
Still, where are they taking us?

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:14.430
If they're taking you away in a security car,

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:16.550
there's only one place it could be.

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:25.290
The five we arrested will arrive shortly.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:30.650
Put the girl who uses Fusion 
Summoning in a separate cell.

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:33.420
Once she calms down, I'll interrogate her myself.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:38.040
Don't put the remaining four with the other prisoners.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.360
Keep them under supervision separately.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:42.170
Yes, sir.

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:48.070
We have plenty of time to deal 
with them, one by one.

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:50.580
All right... I'm home free.

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:57.160
Hey! We were told not to keep the five 
arriving prisoners in the shared cells,

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:59.010
but separate, under supervision.

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:00.830
Did you hear me?

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:03.240
And a girl among them needs a special cell.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:04.380
Right!

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:05.660
I said don't forget!

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:08.330
Yeah, yeah. I've got it.

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:18.920
We're bringing in five prisoners.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:19.730
Acknowledged.

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:21.030
Prisoners?

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:23.040
I'm Shingo Sawatari! You're going to—

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:25.530
No one cares. Pipe down.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:29.600
You're to be separated from the other four.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:30.910
Come with me.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:33.780
It's all right. Don't make a fuss.

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:37.560
Come on, we'll go this way.

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:42.250
We're confiscating your disks.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:44.390
Duels are off-limits without permission.

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:46.860
But you can take this.

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:49.330
You aren't confiscating our decks?

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:52.800
In here, that's worth almost as much as your life.

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:55.400
Well, take care of them, okay?

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:01.320
Welcome to the dead end for deadbeats like you.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:10.250
I doubt we'll be getting fluffy beds 
or full course meals here.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:13.080
With a few exceptions,

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:18.560
everyone here is a Common, arrested for 
being a potential dissident.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:22.270
Hundreds have been held here on false charges.

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:23.470
False charges?

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:25.000
You mean like us?

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:29.290
Yeah. But there are two types of people here.

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:30.320
Two types?

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:30.970
Yeah.

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:33.480
Those whose eyes are dead.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:36.120
And those whose eyes aren't dead.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:49.190
From now on, this shared cell 
will be your happy home.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:52.740
I'm sure you'll get along with the other trash here.

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:56.800
Happy home, my eye!

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:01.790
Shared cell? I feel like I was 
told something about that...

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:03.030
Well, whatever.

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:06.240
Well, then, what do we do now?

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:09.570
Oh, newcomers?

00:07:11.590 --> 00:07:13.560
Aren't you going to say hello?

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:16.400
H-Hello, there...

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:18.620
A proper greeting...

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:21.040
...would be to prostrate yourself 
on the ground and say,

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.090
"I'm at your service, sir."

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:26.060
Why should I do that?

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:29.870
If you want me to sit, you should produce a sofa.

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:30.750
What?

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:31.720
Damn you!

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.770
Don't be so vulgar!

00:07:36.110 --> 00:07:38.490
Gongenzaka? What are you doing he—

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:41.770
Yuya! You're safe?!

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:43.840
Hey, Gongenzaka... Can't brea—

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:45.560
I thought I'd never see you again.

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.500
To think we'd meet here, of all places!

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:50.270
The man, Gongen... Gongen...

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:54.880
Who's this overbearing weirdo?

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:57.660
Oh, Gonny, you're overreacting.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:00.360
I told you we'd find him soon enough.

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:02.560
Hello, Yuya!

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:05.260
Dennis! You're here, too?

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:10.440
Yeah, when they caught us, I was dueling 
Kurosaki in an underground venue.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:11.670
Kurosaki's here, too?

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:14.220
Yeah, and he's well enough for now.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:15.140
For now?

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:17.150
The same day they brought us in,

00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:22.080
he got in a fight with ten other prisoners, 
and they threw him in solitary.

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:25.770
You know these guys, Boss Gon?

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:30.010
Yeah, this man is Yuya Sakaki, my best friend.

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:34.480
And that's Sawatari. We're not particularly close.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:37.400
Boss Gon's best friend...

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:38.920
...and a distant acquaintance?!

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:42.000
We're sorry! We're sorry! We're sorry!

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.670
U-Um, it isn't a big deal.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:48.870
By the way, Yuya, where are Reiji 
Akaba and our other comrades?

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:50.890
Layra's safe.

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:53.810
By now, he's probably with Reiji Akaba.

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:55.310
And Yuzu...

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:57.520
What? You saw Yuzu?

00:08:57.860 --> 00:09:01.640
No, not yet. But she seems to be nearby.

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:04.720
We need to get out of here fast, to get to searching!

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:08.460
Aren't you the big boss here? Can't you do something?

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:10.680
I'm not really the boss.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:12.990
The big boss of the prison is somewhere else.

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:15.750
I hear he's been in for ten years.

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:28.910
Huh? That's all?

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:31.400
We're starting to run low.

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:34.320
Give me a break! You still have a ton!

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:35.880
Keep moving!

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.050
You're holding up the line.

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:38.560
Quit complaining and eat!

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:40.790
Yeah, move along.

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:44.280
Hey.

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:47.720
I am the great Shingo Sawatari.

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:50.380
Go ahead and mess with me the same way.

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:55.370
I'll tell my daddy, and he'll make you all regret it.

00:09:56.790 --> 00:09:58.570
D-Damn it...

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:01.360
In the end, all four of us are 
treated the same way?

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:03.480
It doesn't matter. Let's just eat.

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:07.220
Honestly. I don't have to deal 
with this absurd treatment...

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:14.920
Was that a card?

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:17.450
Yuya, what are you doing? Let's go!

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:18.760
O-Okay.

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:23.800
Yuya!

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:25.900
Oh, what a waste!

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:27.770
You've gotta be careful where you walk.

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:31.780
Whoops!

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:37.050
Sorry, sorry...

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:39.350
It was only because he was lying on the floor.

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:43.590
This was waste water from 
cleaning the lavatories, too.

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:44.840
Why, you...

00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:46.240
He's mocking us!

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:47.560
Hey, you!

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:50.140
If you fight, you'll be thrown in solitary.

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:51.530
Get it cleaned up!

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:53.210
You four.

00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:56.220
Don't protest any more.

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:58.730
We'll split our dinners with you.

00:10:58.730 --> 00:10:59.870
And look over there.

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:07.660
He's the boss.

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:08.550
What?

00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:10.540
He's the boss?

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:11.640
Yuya!

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:12.730
Are you okay?

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:13.990
Y-Yeah.

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:16.950
He does seem better off than the rest.

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:20.780
The prison boss wields more 
power than the guards.

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:36.670
Okay, you're going to clean this 
place until it sparkles.

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:38.240
Now?

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:43.650
Hold it! We just finished washing 
all the prisoners' dishes!

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:45.760
Just do it.

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:49.390
Cleaning the showers is work 
for newbies who just arrived.

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:53.400
And let me warn you, the boiler's been shut off.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:57.360
If you try to take a shower while you clean, 
you'll get nothing but cold water.

00:11:57.360 --> 00:12:01.540
Um, I've been a bit under the weather all day...

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:03.170
A card?

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:05.960
I've got muscle pain.

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:07.450
I've been malnourished.

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:09.020
I've been tired.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:16.750
Okay, you can go back.

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:18.780
Thank you!

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:21.380
You four, take care of it.

00:12:22.870 --> 00:12:25.120
Hey! This is really fishy!

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:28.760
Listen up... If it isn't done right, 
we'll make you do it again.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:29.590
Wait!

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:32.060
Damn... What's going on?

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:33.820
Didn't they tell you?

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:36.530
Cards are almost as valuable as your lives.

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:40.880
In this place, cards act like money.

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:44.240
You can bribe the jailers with 
cards for better treatment.

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:47.080
That's why they returned our decks?

00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:51.880
Now that I know, I wish I'd traded 
a card to get a decent meal.

00:12:51.880 --> 00:12:54.590
Sawatari! Cards aren't money!

00:12:54.590 --> 00:12:57.360
Using them to get preferential treatment...

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:01.160
Don't tell me... You two already did it?

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:03.210
You used cards to buy things?

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:06.000
Gongenzaka!

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:08.330
You used your cards for something like that?!

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:09.440
No!

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:12.270
Boss Gon had no choice...

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:13.500
He did it for us.

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:16.470
There's no need to tell him that.

00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:18.800
No, let us tell him!

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:23.180
Before we came here, we'd lost a 
duel and had our decks taken,

00:13:23.180 --> 00:13:24.950
so we didn't have a single card.

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:28.100
Because of that, we were bullied so badly!

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.620
And so, Boss Gon went to a jailer and said...

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:38.890
Wh-What?

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:41.430
Cards.

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:44.900
Now, let those two eat!

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:47.330
If not for that...

00:13:47.330 --> 00:13:48.580
Right now we'd...

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:50.840
Dennis also gave up his cards.

00:13:52.570 --> 00:13:56.280
Let those two in, as often as they want. Okay?

00:13:56.790 --> 00:14:00.020
I didn't like Gonny getting all the attention!

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:01.960
I see.

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:06.490
But I still think using cards this way is wrong.

00:14:06.930 --> 00:14:08.820
Yeah, I agree.

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:12.700
You've been called. Get out.

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:14.060
Called?

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:24.040
There, you are. This is a personal invitation 
from the big boss, Tokumatsu.

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:25.740
Tokumatsu?

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:28.800
A personal invitation? You must think 
you're really something!

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:29.710
What was that?!

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:32.940
Don't make trouble now, okay?

00:14:32.940 --> 00:14:34.560
It'd be more trouble than it's worth.

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:37.150
Hand them over.

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:39.770
Your cards! He means your cards!

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:40.590
Our cards?

00:14:40.590 --> 00:14:43.630
If you want to enjoy your lives here, 
hand them over.

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:45.100
No way!

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:46.560
What?

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:49.440
I refuse, as well.

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:52.440
The man, Gongenzaka, has not a single card

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:56.760
to spare for appeasing your boss!

00:14:56.760 --> 00:15:00.480
We need to get out of here, as soon as possible.

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:03.680
We don't intend to enjoy our lives here!

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:05.850
B-Bro...

00:15:05.850 --> 00:15:07.920
It's okay. Keep quiet.

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:11.390
Listen up... I am the big boss here.

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:13.100
In other words, the guy in charge.

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:15.240
I make the rules.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:18.120
You people at the bottom serve me.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:20.530
That's how things work in this world.

00:15:20.840 --> 00:15:24.190
I refuse! Cards exist to be used in duels!

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:26.800
Unreasonable brats...

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:28.470
Then, look at this!

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:38.050
What's that?

00:15:42.110 --> 00:15:45.290
Do you know what this is?

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:49.980
These are the cards I've taken, over ten 
years, from those who have lost to me.

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:52.330
From duelists who lost?

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:55.080
Cards are proof of status here.

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:57.070
Duels are proof of power!

00:15:57.070 --> 00:15:58.700
Proof of power?

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:01.310
No! Duels are meant to be enjoyed!

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:02.770
What?

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:05.240
Enjoyed?

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:09.530
Boss, this idiot is saying he's 
going to enjoy his duels here!

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:13.720
Stop laughing like a fool!

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:15.450
S-Sorry!

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:18.620
If you'd just obeyed, I'd intended 
to take it easy on you.

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:20.200
But I've changed my mind.

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:21.190
Jailer!

00:16:21.190 --> 00:16:23.530
Yes, yes? What is it, sir?

00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:28.810
Bring duel disks. We're having a duel here.

00:16:29.370 --> 00:16:31.440
Th-This is a rare card...

00:16:31.440 --> 00:16:33.840
Yes, sir. At once.

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:37.660
Even in hell, cards determine your fate.

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:41.260
Since I can't seem to explain, 
I'll have to demonstrate.

00:16:41.260 --> 00:16:44.820
Are you ready? I'll beat the 
truth into you with a duel!

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:47.520
Bring it on!

00:16:49.990 --> 00:16:52.000
You don't understand.

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:54.960
Those who turn against the elites 
will always be crushed.

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:57.620
I'm the one who'll decide whether I'm crushed!

00:16:58.130 --> 00:16:59.480
Brat...

00:16:59.480 --> 00:17:00.470
Let's go!

00:17:01.180 --> 00:17:02.090
Duel!

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:10.790
Hey, that stance...

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:13.780
Yeah, I've seen him somewhere before.

00:17:14.180 --> 00:17:15.450
My turn.

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:18.520
I activate spell card Flower Gathering from my hand.

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:23.220
Its effect lets me Special Summon four 
Flower Cardians, with 100 attack points,

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:25.820
from my deck in attack position.

00:17:28.290 --> 00:17:34.270
I summon Flower Cardian Pine, 
Zebra Grass, Willow, and Paulownia!

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:37.000
He summoned four at once!

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:41.240
And I activate my spell card Flower 
Stacking from my hand!

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:47.390
This card lets me choose three Flower 
Cardian monsters from my deck,

00:17:47.390 --> 00:17:51.040
and put them on top of my 
deck in the order I choose.

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:55.100
I choose Flower Cardian Pine with Crane, 
Zebra Grass with Moon,

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:57.740
and Paulownia with Phoenix!

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:03.890
Then I activate the effect of Flower Cardian 
Pine with Crane in my hand!

00:18:04.280 --> 00:18:08.570
It allows me to tribute Pine, to Special 
Summon it from my hand!

00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:13.200
Then, when I've successfully 
Special Summoned this card,

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:15.570
I can draw another!

00:18:15.910 --> 00:18:19.210
I drew Zebra Grass with Moon, 
and I activate its effect!

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:22.580
By tributing Zebra Grass, I Special 
Summon this card.

00:18:24.770 --> 00:18:28.640
By successfully Special Summoning it, 
I can draw another card!

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:32.490
And I activate the effect of Paulownia 
with Phoenix that I drew!

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:35.900
I tribute Paulownia, to Special Summon this card.

00:18:36.690 --> 00:18:41.130
Having successfully Special Summoned it, 
I can draw another card!

00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:44.940
And I activate the effect of Willow with 
Calligrapher that I drew!

00:18:45.410 --> 00:18:48.640
I tribute Willow, to Special Summon this card!

00:18:48.910 --> 00:18:52.110
The successful Special Summon 
lets me draw one more card!

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:54.150
Amazing!

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:57.850
Just like that, he has four monsters, 
with 2000 attack points, on his field!

00:18:58.290 --> 00:19:01.550
I drew Cardian Cherry Blossom with Curtain.

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:04.260
But I have no Cherry Blossom card on my field...

00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:07.220
Therefore, this card is sent to my graveyard.

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:11.660
But it isn't over yet.

00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:13.130
I'm only getting started!

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:16.460
Willow with Calligrapher's effect activates!

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:18.750
When this card is used as a Synchro component,

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:21.540
all my monsters become Level 2!

00:19:23.110 --> 00:19:27.820
Here it comes! Level 2 Willow with Calligrapher 
tunes Cardian Pine with Crane,

00:19:27.820 --> 00:19:32.620
Moon with Zebra Grass, and Phoenix with Paulownia!

00:19:34.780 --> 00:19:39.510
Rain of tears! Turn to light and rain down!

00:19:40.460 --> 00:19:42.330
Synchro Summon!

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:48.530
Come out, Level 8 Flower Cardian Lightshower!

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:55.640
He managed to even Synchro 
Summon on his first turn?

00:19:55.640 --> 00:19:58.960
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:02.010
Boy, let me tell you once more!

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:05.620
Cards are proof of status. Duels are proof of power!

00:20:05.980 --> 00:20:09.040
No matter how many times you tell me, 
it won't change what I believe!

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:10.940
Duels are meant to be enjoyed.

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:12.090
My turn!

00:20:12.090 --> 00:20:13.980
You are a fool, boy.

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:16.140
Lightshower's effect activates!

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:19.930
When you draw, it deals 1500 damage to you!

00:20:22.770 --> 00:20:24.140
What?

00:20:24.140 --> 00:20:27.500
Then, every time Yuya draws, 
he'll take massive damage?!

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:30.240
Then he just has to defeat the card before then?

00:20:30.710 --> 00:20:34.400
You aren't the only one who can summon 
multiple monsters at once!

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:35.210
What?

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:39.740
I set the Pendulum Scale with Scale 3 
Performapal Bit Bite Turtle

00:20:39.740 --> 00:20:44.250
and Scale 8 Timegazer Magician!

00:20:53.440 --> 00:20:57.670
Oh? You can use this summoning method?

00:20:58.140 --> 00:21:02.040
Now, I can summon monsters between 
Levels 4 and 7 simultaneously!

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:03.740
Simultaneously?

00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:06.710
Swing, my soul's pendulum!

00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:09.680
Draw an arc of light in the sky!

00:21:10.030 --> 00:21:11.450
Pendulum Summon!

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:13.960
Come out, my monsters!

00:21:17.070 --> 00:21:20.020
First, Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:21:22.440 --> 00:21:25.500
Then Performapal Teeter Totter Hopper!

00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:28.970
And one more! Performapal Sellshell Crab!

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:33.200
Continuous Trap Fraud Freeze!

00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:36.970
This card activates when you Special 
Summon a monster from your hand,

00:21:36.970 --> 00:21:38.940
and returns that monster to your hand.

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:39.880
What?

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:43.120
My god!

00:21:43.120 --> 00:21:46.320
The big Pendulum Summon he managed 
was treated as a fraud!

00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:50.750
As long as he has that trap card, Pendulum Summoning 
will be treated as fraudulent?

00:21:50.750 --> 00:21:54.220
And Tokumatsu has Lightshower on the field.

00:21:54.220 --> 00:21:57.490
Each time Yuya draws, it deals 1500 damage to him.

00:21:58.200 --> 00:21:59.230
Yuya...

00:22:00.560 --> 00:22:05.170
It appears duels have changed a lot 
in the ten years I've been in here.

00:22:05.440 --> 00:22:08.410
But I've been undefeated for those same ten years,

00:22:08.410 --> 00:22:10.770
and I won't bend to you!

00:23:49.640 --> 00:23:51.410
I will not draw.

00:23:51.410 --> 00:23:52.410
What?

00:23:52.720 --> 00:23:56.250
You won't draw? Then how will you duel?

00:23:56.250 --> 00:23:58.830
This Lightshower's effect...

00:23:58.830 --> 00:24:03.570
The next time you draw, you'll take 1500 damage.

00:24:03.570 --> 00:24:07.420
If you don't want to be drenched by the 
rain of tears, prepare an umbrella!

00:24:08.790 --> 00:24:13.400
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
The Man Who Abandoned the Draw.

00:24:13.400 --> 00:24:15.130
The fun is only getting started!
